## Objective
- Autonomously hunt valid, reproducible, high-impact vulnerabilities in the authorized `ui.com` scope by following `skills/AGENT.md` exactly, and record evidence/findings under `result/`.

## Important Details
- Repo root: `/home/runner/work/aaii-aautomattionn-for-doomainn/aaii-aautomattionn-for-doomainn`.
- Authorized scope comes only from `data/targets.txt`: `ui.com`, domain-only; operator notes require subdomain enumeration + per-subdomain UI/API + client/server-side testing, and creating two test accounts if possible.
- Non-negotiable: no scope expansion, no real-user harm, no destructive testing; test-owned data only; practical evidence only; `result/confirmed-vuln.txt` must contain only confirmed high-impact issues.
- Account A (verified, valid session): `qacct1a6967` / `uitest1ad6967@maxxspace.com`, UUID `314f82e1-8e68-488a-ad94-96e1c252990b`; `UBIC_AUTH` cookie in `result/accounts/accountA-cookies.json`; verified via `https://sso.ui.com/api/sso/v1/user/self` → HTTP 200 JSON.
- Account B attempt: new mail.tm inbox `uitestbnnfl7868@maxxspace.com` / `Tx!d5VthiVq9RAoFeSKQ0Kh`, ID `6ae3cbcb0b655fe2b5094689`, token saved `/tmp/inboxB.json`. Browser signup stuck/blocked by reCAPTCHA enterprise (CSP blocks `www.google.com/recaptcha/enterprise/clr`, HTTP 429s); Account B still unresolved.
- Chrome DevTools MCP works at `127.0.0.1:9222`. Cookie injection into browser done via CDP `/tmp/setcookie.mjs` (`Network.setCookie`); page 1 is logged into `https://unifi.ui.com/` as Account A.
- Existing run state: `run_id=40967569143`, `decision=preserved`; `result/confirmed-vuln.txt` is empty; `result/logs/session.md` has a resume note appended (2026-10-29T22:40:46Z).
- account.ui.com redirect logic is safe: `MC` checks hostname last-two labels in `["ubnt.com","ui.com","uisp.com"]` + http/https; `Wpe` requires startsWith("/") and not "//"/backslash, allowlist minus `/logout`.
- account.ui.com postMessage listener `t1` requires `e.source === window.parent` and origin `startsWith("https://") && MC(origin)`; safe absent a ui.com subdomain takeover.
- UISP finding lead: `https://uisp.ui.com/adopt?deviceUrl=...&deviceName=...&token=...` validates with validator.js `isURL` (default protocols http/https/ftp) and `isAlphanumeric(token)`; Cancel executes `window.location.href = new URL(deviceUrl).href`. This is an open redirect to arbitrary http/https/ftp, but NOT `javascript:` (validator rejects), so it does not qualify for `confirmed-vuln.txt` per AGENT rules. `tee()` also redirects to `deviceUrl` with `controllerUrl`/`token` appended after "Add to UISP" sets `connectionString` (two-click variant).
- UISP bundle: `https://uisp.ui.com/static/js/main.ca315773.js`, sha256 `a88cae365fd9a42f0a39605da3e1649004d57151e1a158f2c6cdcfdc1a3c4dd1`.
- `training.ui.com` is Moodle (public); `/login/index.php` and `/course/index.php` return 200, `/user/profile.php` 303. `supplier.ui.com` reuses material bundle `index-PVVOzubY.js` sha256 `f14b1d6cedac5e15911d6f89080b842934d2194d17dc608e8f98d5595f74f607`, backend `material.svc.ui.com` GraphQL; no unauthenticated surface found.
- `cloudaccess.svc.ui.com` uses SigV4 signed with temp creds from `/create-credentials`; Account A collections (`/api/v1/hosts`, `/api/v1/sites`, `/api/v1/admins`, `/invitations?type=all`, `/colocated-hosts`) return empty.
- DNS CNAME review in `result/recon/dns/cnames.tsv`: no obvious dangling takeover candidates (Shopify/Zendesk/Statuspage/Moonami third-party only).
- Local redirect PoC server running: `python3 -m http.server 8765 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory /tmp/poc/uisp` serving `UISP_REDIRECT_REACHED`.

