SHA-256: a88cae365fd9a42f0a39605da3e1649004d57151e1a158f2c6cdcfdc1a3c4dd1

Observation 1 (confirmed open redirect, http/https/ftp only):
- Loaded:
  https://uisp.ui.com/adopt?deviceUrl=http%3A%2F%2F127.0.0.1%3A8765%2F&deviceName=TESTDEVICE123&token=abc123
- The page rendered "Add device 127.0.0.1 to your UISP?" with a Cancel button.
- Clicking Cancel changed the top-level URL to http://127.0.0.1:8765/,
  which returned the marker page UISP_REDIRECT_REACHED.
- Evidence screenshots:
  01-adopt-page-with-attacker-deviceUrl.png
  02-cancel-redirected-to-local-server.png

Observation 2 (javascript: rejected, so this is NOT XSS):
- Loaded deviceUrl=javascript:document.title='UISPXSS'
  Result: app rejected input and redirected to https://uisp.ui.com/setup;
  document.title remained "UISP Portal". No script execution.
- Loaded deviceUrl=%09javascript:document.title='TABXSS' (leading tab)
  Result: same rejection; no script execution.
- Static analysis: validator.js isURL() default protocols are
  http, https, ftp (require_valid_protocol=true); javascript: is rejected
  before the sink executes.

Sink (minified bundle):
  Cancel button onClick:
    onClick:function(){const e=new URL(s);window.location.href=e.href}
  where s = URLSearchParams.get("deviceUrl").

Related code-level concern (UNRESOLVED, not confirmed):
- The same component executes tee(s,a,d) when connectionString `a` is present:
    function tee(e,t,r){const n=new URL(e);
      n.searchParams.append("controllerUrl",t);
      n.searchParams.append("token",r);window.location.href=n.href}
- "Add to UISP" triggers:
    GET https://unms-go.ubnt.com/api/installations/unifi-controllers/<id>/connection-string
  and stores the response as connectionString. The subsequent render calls
  tee(), sending that controller connection string to the attacker-controlled
  deviceUrl as the controllerUrl query parameter.
- Could not verify end-to-end because Account A has no UISP controllers
  (list-controllers returns {"controllers":[]}) and creating a paid/cloud
  controller trial was intentionally not performed.
EOF
