## Objective
- Autonomously hunt valid, reproducible, high-impact vulnerabilities in the authorized `ui.com` scope by following `skills/AGENT.md` exactly, and record evidence/findings under `result/`.

## Important Details
- Repo root: `/home/runner/work/aaii-aautomattionn-for-doomainn/aaii-aautomattionn-for-doomainn`.
- Authorized scope comes only from `data/targets.txt`: `ui.com`, domain-only; operator notes require subdomain enumeration + per-subdomain UI/API + client/server-side testing, and creating two test accounts if possible.
- Non-negotiable: no scope expansion, no real-user harm, no destructive testing; test-owned data only; practical evidence only; `result/confirmed-vuln.txt` must contain only confirmed high-impact issues.
- Account A (verified, valid session): `qacct1a6967` / `uitest1ad6967@maxxspace.com`, UUID `314f82e1-8e68-488a-ad94-96e1c252990b`; `UBIC_AUTH` cookie in `result/accounts/accountA-cookies.json`; verified via `https://sso.ui.com/api/sso/v1/user/self` → HTTP 200 JSON.
- Account B attempt: new mail.tm inbox `uitestbnnfl7868@maxxspace.com` / `Tx!d5VthiVq9RAoFeSKQ0Kh`, ID `6ae3cbcb0b655fe2b5094689`, token in `/tmp/inboxB.json`. Browser signup still blocked by reCAPTCHA enterprise; retry in `isolatedContext=accountB2` showed reCAPTCHA iframe, `Create Account` disabled, no `POST /api/sso/v2/users`, inbox count 0.
- Account B is still unresolved; do not bypass/solve CAPTCHA.
- Chrome DevTools MCP works at `127.0.0.1:9222`. Cookie injection via CDP `/tmp/setcookie.mjs` (`Network.setCookie`).
- Current browser pages: page 1 = `https://unifi.ui.com/` as Account A with the “Qa 1” account dialog open; page 2 = `https://account.ui.com/login?...` (`isolatedContext=accountB`); page 3 = `https://account.ui.com/register` (`isolatedContext=accountB2`, submit disabled).
- Existing run state: `run_id=40967569143`, `decision=preserved`; `result/confirmed-vuln.txt` still only the empty template/comments.
- account.ui.com redirect logic is safe: `MC` checks hostname last-two labels in `["ubnt.com","ui.com","uisp.com"]` + http/https; `Wpe` requires startsWith("/") and not "//"/backslash, allowlist minus `/logout`.
- account.ui.com postMessage listener `t1` requires `e.source === window.parent` and origin `startsWith("https://") && MC(origin)`; safe absent a ui.com subdomain takeover.
- UISP finding: `https://uisp.ui.com/adopt?deviceUrl=...&deviceName=...&token=...` validates with validator.js `isURL` (defaults http/https/ftp) and `isAlphanumeric(token)`; Cancel executes `window.location.href = new URL(deviceUrl).href`. Confirmed open redirect to http/https/ftp, but `javascript:` rejected → excluded from `confirmed-vuln.txt`.
- UISP bundle used for analysis: `https://uisp.ui.com/home/static/js/main.ca315773.js` (also `/tmp/uisp/main.js`), sha256 `a88cae365fd9a42f0a39605da3e1649004d57151e1a158f2c6cdcfdc1a3c4dd1`.
- UISP code-level lead (unresolved): after “Add to UISP” sets `connectionString` via `GET https://unms-go.ubnt.com/api/installations/unifi-controllers/<id>/connection-string`, `tee(s,a,d)` appends `controllerUrl=<connectionString>&token=<token>` to attacker-controlled `deviceUrl` and redirects. Account A has no controllers (`list-controllers` returns `{"controllers":[]}`), so end-to-end not verified.
- `artifacts.ui.com`, `nca.ui.com`, `microsites.ui.com` all load the UniFi Site Manager shell for Account A but show “Access Prohibited”; `enterprise.svc.ui.com/api/v2/organizations` returns `{"data":[]}`.
- `cloudaccess.svc.ui.com` requires SigV4; direct curl gets 403. Account A hosts/sites/invitations are empty.
- JWT tests negative: `UBIC_AUTH` is RS256; `alg:none` (with/without signature) and HS256 signed with the RSA public key both return 401 ` is not allowed`.
- CORS test negative: `sso.ui.com/api/sso/v1/user/self` only returns `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: https://uisp.ui.com` (+ credentials) for the valid origin; `https://evil.example`/`null` get no ACAO.
- Headers: account.ui.com CSP includes `frame-ancestors 'self' *.ui.com uic.uidev.tools *.uic.uidev.tools`; `uic.uidev.tools` is out of scope. `x-frame-options: SAMEORIGIN`.
- New in-scope hosts discovered via app links: `activate.ui.com` (200 static SPA), `activate.stg.ui.com` (403 CloudFront), `team.df.ui.com/portal/manage-account` (200, “UID Enterprise Workspace”).
- UID Enterprise config in `/tmp/teamdf/6459.dbe916f7.js`: `base=https://api-gw.uid.df.ui.com`, `core-api_gw=https://core-api-gw.uid.df.ui.com`, `core-login=https://core-web-login.uid.df.ui.com`, `msp-portal=https://pro.uid.df.ui.com`, `login=https://login.uid.df.ui.com`, `portal=https://portal.uid.df.ui.com`, `www=https://www.uid.df.ui.com`, `env:"df"`, `domain:".ui.com"`; also `identity.df.ui.com`, `cloud.uid.df.ui.com`, `status.uid.df.ui.com`, `status.uid.ui.com`.
- UID gateway probes: `core-api-gw.uid.df.ui.com/` → `{"code":"SUCCESS","data":{"status":"UP"}}`; most paths → 404 `{"code":404,"msg":"you entered no-man zone"}`. `api-gw.uid.df.ui.com/api-gateway/api/server/status` → 200 `{"msg":"","data":{"timestamp":...},"code":"SUCCESS"}`. `core-api-gw.../core-status/api/v1/public/maintain?cell_name=cell0` → `{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":"success","data":{"maintain":false}}`; missing `cell_name` → 422 `{"code":602,"message":"cell_name in query is required"}`.
- Extracted UID endpoints include `/account/*`, `/admin/*`, `/user/*`, `/auth/*`, `/idp/*`, `/authn/api/v1`, `/workflow/api/v1`, `/announcement/api/v1`, `/api/v2/user/oauth2`, `/api/v2/transpond/webrtc`, `/api/v2/ws/signaling`; unauth testing not yet done.
- UID Enterprise signup seems gated; JS error strings include “UID Enterprise is temporarily not accepting new workspace signup” and workspace-registration errors. Avoid email-sending endpoints (`/auth/email/send`).
- `training.ui.com` is Moodle (public); `/login/index.php` and `/course/index.php` 200, `/user/profile.php` 303. No version identified.
- `supplier.ui.com` reuses material bundle `index-PVVOzubY.js`, backend `material.svc.ui.com` GraphQL; no unauthenticated surface found.
- DNS CNAME review in `result/recon/dns/cnames.tsv`: no obvious dangling takeover candidates.
- Local redirect PoC server still running: pid `5577`, `python3 -m http.server 8765 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory /tmp/poc/uisp`, serving `UISP_REDIRECT_REACHED`.

