===== SUMMARY.md =====
# Run Summary

- Run: `40967569143` (schedule), decision `preserved`
- Scope: `ui.com` domain only, per `data/targets.txt`
- Time spent: ~5h20m (start `2026-10-29T17:37:02Z`; resumed `22:40:46Z`)
- Confirmed high-impact vulnerabilities: **none**
- Excluded candidate: `VULN-20261029-001` (UISP `/adopt` open redirect)

## Tested surface

- Recon: 77 live subdomains, HTTP probing/header capture, CNAME review for
  dangling-takeover candidates. No obvious takeover candidate.
- account.ui.com: login/register, redirect (`MC`/`Wpe`) and postMessage origin
  checks, JWT algorithm-confusion tests (`UBIC_AUTH` RS256; `alg:none` and
  HS256-with-public-key rejected 401), security headers.
- sso.ui.com: `/api/sso/v1/user/self`, CORS origin reflection (only
  `https://uisp.ui.com` reflected), user/self IDOR probes.
- unifi.ui.com / artifacts.ui.com / nca.ui.com / microsites.ui.com /
  enterprise.svc.ui.com: Account A session; all show “Access Prohibited” and no
  org/console data.
- uisp.ui.com: `/adopt` device-adoption flow, URL/query validation, Cancel
  navigation sink, controller/connection-string flow, mock-controller attempts.
- community.ui.com: anonymous and Account A API probes (users, notifications,
  feed, member groups, content-risk reviews, escalations, admin integration
  users).
- design.ui.com, supplier.ui.com / material.svc.ui.com, training.ui.com
  (Moodle), var.ui.com, directrma.ui.com / rma.ui.com, cloudaccess.svc.ui.com:
  bundle/route review and unauthenticated probing.
- UID Enterprise dev surface: `team.df.ui.com`, `login.uid.df.ui.com`,
  `portal.uid.df.ui.com`, `api-gw.uid.df.ui.com`,
  `core-api-gw.uid.df.ui.com`; public status endpoints and JS route/endpoint
  inventory.
- Store/community/status/blog/careers hosts: platform checks (Shopify,
  Atlassian, CloudFront) and redirects; not deeply tested.

## Confirmed findings

None met the high-impact notification bar. `result/confirmed-vuln.txt` is
empty by design.

`VULN-20261029-001`: UISP `/adopt` Cancel follows an attacker-controlled
`deviceUrl` (http/https/ftp) to an external origin. Confirmed in-browser, but
`javascript:` is rejected by validator.js `isURL`, so impact is limited to an
open redirect. Full report and exclusion rationale in
`result/findings/VULN-20261029-001/report.md`.

## Unresolved

See `result/unresolved.md`. Main blockers:

- Account B signup blocked by reCAPTCHA enterprise; cross-account IDOR/BOLA
  untested.
- UISP connection-string exfiltration lead not provable without a controller
  (no paid trial created).
- UID Enterprise workspace signup gated; no enterprise credentials, so its
  authenticated API/auth surface remains untested.
- CloudFront/SigV4/third-party hosts inaccessible or outside intended app
  surface.

===== scope.md =====
# Scope

## Target entries and classification

- `ui.com` — domain-only target (from `data/targets.txt`).
- Operator notes explicitly request: enumerate valid/interesting subdomains, save them to a text file, then test each discovered subdomain individually for UI routes, API endpoints, client-side and server-side issues.

## User Instructions

Restated from `data/targets.txt`:

1. Identify valid and potentially interesting subdomains of ui.com and save them in a text file.
2. Test each discovered subdomain individually.
3. For each subdomain, discover all UI routes and API endpoints first.
4. Then test for both client-side and server-side vulnerabilities.
5. Do not ask questions; make reasonable independent decisions.
6. First try to create two test accounts on the target subdomain and save their credentials in a file for testing. If account creation is not possible, test only unauthenticated endpoints.
7. Final goal: identify valid, impactful, reportable vulnerabilities.

These notes are followed only within the safe, authorized interpretation below.

## Authorization source / assumptions

- Authorized scope comes from `data/targets.txt` (`ui.com`).
- Subdomains of `ui.com` are treated as explicitly approved components because the operator notes explicitly instruct subdomain discovery and per-subdomain testing.
- Scope does NOT extend to sibling/registrable domains, third-party services, CDNs, partner systems, or unrelated origins. Any discovered asset not under `ui.com` is recorded in `result/out-of-scope.txt` and not tested.
- `creds/test-account.txt` contains BytePlus console credentials for `console.byteplus.com`, which is NOT in `data/`. They are out of scope and are not used on ui.com.

## In-scope components

- `ui.com` and discovered subdomains resolving under `ui.com`, subject to the safety rules in `skills/AGENT.md` Section 2.

## Explicitly out-of-scope components

- Any non-`ui.com` domain (including byteplus.com and console.byteplus.com).
- Third-party CDNs/analytics/payment providers and their origins.
- Anything requiring destructive testing, real-user data, DoS, brute force, or high-volume fuzzing.

## Program restrictions discovered

- No formal program policy file was provided in `data/` or `vulnebleti/`.
- Binding safety restrictions from `skills/AGENT.md`: test-owned data only, no destructive/disruptive tests, respect rate limits, no real-user harm, no account creation where prohibited, practical evidence only.
- Account creation will only be attempted through normal public signup using disposable test identities if such a flow exists and behaves safely; otherwise unauthenticated testing only.

===== unresolved.md =====
# Unresolved items

- **Account B / cross-account IDOR & BOLA tests** — second public signup hit
  `403 CHALLENGE_RECAPTCHA_TOKEN_REQUIRED` followed by an interactive reCAPTCHA
  image challenge. No second authenticated identity is available, so tests that
  require two accounts are marked Unresolved.
- **Account B registration mass-assignment test** — same CAPTCHA blocker.
- **Hosts returning 000 or 403 on first probe** (beta.community.ui.com,
  security.community.ui.com, docker*.dl.ui.com, crm.trunking.ui.com,
  stg.store.ui.com, community.status.ui.com) were not retried; recorded in
  `result/recon/`.
- **Store/storefront hosts** run on Shopify (third-party platform). Not deeply
  tested because the platform is external and outside the intended application
  surface.
- **UISP `/adopt` connection-string exfiltration (code-level lead)** — `tee()`
  appends `controllerUrl=<connectionString>&token=<token>` to the attacker
  `deviceUrl` and redirects, but `connectionString` is fetched for a controller
  ID. Account A owns no controllers (`list-controllers` returns
  `{"controllers":[]}`); a paid UISP Cloud trial was intentionally not created.
  See `result/findings/VULN-20261029-001/report.md`.
- **UID Enterprise Workspace (`team.df.ui.com`, `login.uid.df.ui.com`,
  `portal.uid.df.ui.com`)** — dev environment discovered via app links. JS
  bundles reveal API gateways `api-gw.uid.df.ui.com`,
  `core-api-gw.uid.df.ui.com`, `core-web-login.uid.df.ui.com`,
  `pro.uid.df.ui.com`, `identity.df.ui.com`, `cloud.uid.df.ui.com`. Public
  status endpoints work; deeper API/auth testing needs a workspace account.
  Signup appears gated ("temporarily not accepting new workspace signup") and
  no workspace credentials exist. Specific untested sink:
  `browserJump`/`handleJump` sets `window.location.href = params.path` from a
  server-provided click object (`index.85133d08.js`), potentially a stored
  open-redirect/XSS if low-priv users can craft such cards.
- **`login.uid.df.ui.com` `from` parameter** — parsed from the query string and
  forwarded as `x-from-url` on `/account/login`; post-auth redirect handling was
  not verifiable without valid enterprise credentials, so open-redirect status
  is unresolved.
- **`activate.ui.com`** — returns a static SPA shell; no unauthenticated API or
  redirect surface identified yet. `activate.stg.ui.com` returns CloudFront 403.
- **CloudFront/SigV4-protected hosts** (`activate.stg.ui.com`,
  `cloudaccess.svc.ui.com`) — cannot test without signed requests / real org.
- **`team.df.ui.com` `df` environment is a non-production dogfood environment**;
  any issue found there should be confirmed against production `uid.ui.com`
  hosts before being treated as high impact.
